{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>ולא תחללו את שם קדשי</b> [you shall not profane My holy name]: He is speaking with the sons of Aaron, for the pericope is continuous and they are the ones commanded not to slaughter for themselves or for Israel a mother and its son on one day. It is also possible that it is a commandment regarding וכי תזבחו זבח תודה [when you slaughter a thanksgiving offering] directed to the priests. And the proof is that he began the pericope with אחר כן דבר אל בני ישראל [then speak to the children of Israel] and concluded with ונקדשתי בתוך בני ישראל [I shall be sanctified among the children of Israel]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:50.310229576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}